{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And these are the children of Anah: Dishon and Oholibamah the daughter of Anah.</b> It is the way of Scripture to state similarly concerning daughters, as in \"and Dinah his daughter\" (Genesis 46:15). This Anah is the fourth son of Seir the Horite, the brother of Zibeon, who is counted after him above (Genesis 36:20), for the section counts seven sons of Seir the Horite as their generations. This Anah had one son who is also called Dishon, like the name of his uncle, and he had a daughter called Oholibamah, like the name of her relative Oholibamah the daughter of Anah son of Zibeon. Therefore Scripture says concerning the wife of Esau (Genesis 36:2): \"Oholibamah the daughter of Anah, the daughter of Zibeon,\" to make known that she is the daughter of the Anah who found the mules, the granddaughter of Zibeon — not Oholibamah the daughter of Anah son of Seir the Horite, the brother of Zibeon. \n\nNow according to the opinion of some of our Rabbis (Pesahim 54a), there is only one person called Anah in the entire section, and he is the son of Zibeon who came in immorality upon his mother, the wife of Seir the Horite. Scripture counts him (Genesis 36:20) among the sons of Seir the Horite because the people considered him as his son and called him Anah son of Seir, and he raised him among his sons, thinking he was his son. And Scripture counts him another time (Genesis 36:24) according to the truth, as the son of Zibeon. This is the midrash of those who interpret stringently, as mentioned in tractate Pesahim (ibid.), but it is not the opinion of everyone in the Gemara, nor is it the plain sense of Scripture at all:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {0 "The phrase 'who found the mules' (הימים) refers back to Genesis 36:24, where Anah is said to have found the ימים in the wilderness; the term is left untranslated here as Ramban references it elliptically."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:40:29.752736934Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}